        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Fix `display` toggle in playground not changing value]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42437</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42437"/>
        <updated>2025-12-17T10:54:21.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60345799?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Changes a <code class="notranslate">&lt;select&gt;</code> value in a playground to be read after each change of the <code class="notranslate">&lt;select&gt;</code>, correctly reacting to the change.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Display/Multi-keyword_syntax#display_block_flow-root_and_display_inline_flow-root" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">display: flow-root</code> playground</a> has a <code class="notranslate">&lt;select&gt;</code> toggle, which is supposed to change the <code class="notranslate">display</code> value of some elements to demonstrate the effects of the <code class="notranslate">flow-root</code> value.</p>
<p dir="auto">Currently, its value is read only once when the playground JS is first executed, which results in <code class="notranslate">display: block</code> always getting set on the elements.</p>]]></content>
